<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Topasses</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Larantuqueiros, Black Portuguese</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Topasses were a Portuguese-speaking Catholic community of mixed Portuguese, Indian and Southeast Asian descent who dominated much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timor">Timor</a> from the 17th century. Led by the rival Hornay and da Costa families from their base at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lifau">Lifau</a>, they controlled the sandalwood trade and fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kupang">Kupang</a>. Their power declined in the 18th century as Portugal took more direct control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-timor">East Timor</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/topasses.jpg" alt="Topasses" width="320" height="506" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johannes Nieuhof · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_Topas_or_Mardick_with_his_wife.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
